<PublicLayout lang="en" title="Read-only AIS open banking" description="Groowy's roadmap for future read-only AIS partnerships: consent, a regulated provider and no premature partnership claims." canonicalPath="/en/partners/open-banking/" {alternatePaths}>
  <article class="prose"><p class="eyebrow">Partner · roadmap</p><h1>A bridge to accounts, without becoming the bank.</h1><p>Groowy is evaluating read-only AIS access to reduce manual entry and improve financial overviews. Any integration would require explicit consent, a regulated provider and a documented data perimeter.</p><div class="notice">No provider has been selected. This page is not a partnership, does not offer banking access and does not describe an available feature.</div><div class="card"><h2>Roadmap status</h2><p>We are collecting requirements and potential partners; there is no active integration yet. Public technical evidence stays in the <a href="/en/security/">Security and data</a> page.</p></div><h2>What we will verify together</h2><ul><li>institution coverage, data quality and disconnection behaviour;</li><li>understandable consent, revocation, renewal and re-authentication;</li><li>minimisation, retention, deletion and data separation;</li><li>sandbox, limits, documentation and terms suitable for a focused pilot.</li></ul><div class="partner-contact"><p class="eyebrow">First contact</p><h2>Let’s see if there is a good point of connection.</h2><p>To present a service, API or possible collaboration, write to <a href="mailto:hello@groowy.app?subject=Partnership%20Groowy">hello@groowy.app</a>. You can include covered markets, developer documentation, consent model, sandbox and pilot terms.</p><p class="microcopy">This page describes a product direction: Groowy does not claim active banking integrations or its own regulatory authorisations.</p></div></article>
</PublicLayout>
